        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Kimi K2 usage dashboard shortcut",
        "body": "## Summary\n- expose Kimi K2 in the Usage Dashboard submenu\n- directly link the dashboard action to the credits tab (`https://kimi-k2.ai/api/user/credits`)\n\n## Proof\n\nDeterministic test run on this branch (no network, no credentials):\n\n```text\n$ swift test --disable-sandbox --filter 'MenuDescriptorKimiK2Tests|ProviderMetadataStatusLinkTests'\n✔ Test \"kimi K2 metadata identifies the unofficial provider and its dashboard\" passed\n✔ Test \"kimi K2 menu exposes the usage dashboard action\" passed\n✔ Test run with 3 tests in 2 suites passed.\n```\n\nThe Usage Dashboard action resolves to `https://kimi-k2.ai/api/user/credits` — the same host and path the credits fetcher polls — so users land on the balance page this provider actually tracks.\n\n## Codex review follow-up\n\nThe earlier review flagged a host mismatch (dashboard vs. the fetcher's `creditsURL`). The descriptor and metadata now both point at `https://kimi-k2.ai/api/user/credits`, matching `KimiK2UsageFetcher.creditsURL`. A production `MenuDescriptor` test asserts the resolved dashboard URL, and the metadata test was aligned to the same value.\n\n## Testing\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter 'MenuDescriptorKimiK2Tests|ProviderMetadataStatusLinkTests'` (3 passed)\n- `swift build` clean\n",
